# Kernel and live system
linux-image-amd64
live-boot
live-config
live-config-systemd
systemd-sysv
dbus-user-session
sudo
ca-certificates

# Kiosk session: labwc (Wayland, set up as a kiosk in /etc/xdg/oros-labwc)
# + Chromium; wlrctl gives orOS the whole screen back when Claude closes
labwc
wlrctl
chromium
chromium-sandbox
# pkill for the session watchdog
procps
libgl1-mesa-dri
libegl1
mesa-vulkan-drivers
fonts-noto-core
fonts-noto-color-emoji

# Tor button: X apps (Tor Browser) inside labwc, and what checks and
# unpacks the Tor Browser download (oros-system tor)
xwayland
gpgv
xz-utils

# Desktop parts of the session (oros-system desk.go): the screen going off
# and sleep when idle (swayidle; wlopm turns labwc's outputs off), second
# screens (wlr-randr: duplicate, extend, one screen; display.go), PrtSc
# screenshots (grim, through labwc's screencopy), the Orca screen reader
# with local espeak-ng voices through speech-dispatcher (also orOS's
# read-aloud), and the locales Orca speaks in (en, el, de).
swayidle
wlr-randr
wlopm
grim
orca
at-spi2-core
python3-speechd
speech-dispatcher
speech-dispatcher-espeak-ng
espeak-ng
locales

# Network (Wi-Fi from orOS's System button, or nmtui on tty2)
network-manager
wpasupplicant
iw
polkitd

# Screen lock with a fingerprint (oros-system bio.*): fprintd and its tools
fprintd

# System button and installer (oros-system)
efibootmgr
dosfstools
# Disks section: NTFS (Windows) when the kernel driver refuses, exFAT tools
ntfs-3g
exfatprogs
# Problem report: which hardware the computer has
pciutils
e2fsprogs
fdisk

# Clock: NTP from Debian's pool servers, time zones, screen brightness
systemd-timesyncd
tzdata
brightnessctl
# Night Light: real gamma through labwc's wlr-gamma-control (night.go)
wlsunset

# Printing without vendor drivers: CUPS finds IPP Everywhere and AirPrint
# printers on the network (cups-browsed, Avahi) and on USB (ipp-usb).
cups
cups-client
cups-browsed
cups-filters
ipp-usb
ghostscript
avahi-daemon
libnss-mdns
# Scanning for orOS Scan PDF through orOS Bridge (0.9.0+, which loads libsane
# at run time): SANE, and sane-airscan for driverless scanners and
# multifunction printers on the network (eSCL, WSD) and on USB (with ipp-usb)
libsane1
sane-airscan

# Bluetooth: headphones and speakers (PipeWire), mice and keyboards
bluez
libspa-0.2-bluetooth
bluez-firmware

# Boot splash
plymouth
plymouth-themes
# Text on the boot screen: the passphrase prompt of encrypted data
plymouth-label

# Encrypted data (optional, LUKS2): cryptsetup in the system and in the
# initramfs, where oros-unlock asks for the passphrase on the boot screen
cryptsetup
cryptsetup-initramfs
dmsetup

# Sound
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
wireplumber
# orOS Bridge (plugins and the sound card for Studio) reaches PipeWire as a
# PulseAudio client, or through ALSA
libpulse0
# Sound card profiles; without them most laptops show no output at all.
alsa-ucm-conf
alsa-topology-conf

# Firmware for common Wi-Fi, graphics and sound hardware
firmware-linux-free
firmware-linux-nonfree
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-intel-sound
firmware-sof-signed
amd64-microcode
intel-microcode

# Games (G1, 2026-11-22): the system side that Steam, Heroic, itch and
# Lutris need once the software center installs them as Flatpaks from
# Flathub (they bring their own 32-bit libraries and Proton/Wine): Flatpak
# and its portals (file dialogs, the screen staying on), gamemode (the
# processor at full speed while a game runs; pkexec sets the governor),
# Valve's udev rules for controllers and Steam Input (steam-devices,
# contrib), and vulkaninfo for the graphics check and the boot test.
flatpak xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
gamemode pkexec
steam-devices
vulkan-tools

# NVIDIA's own driver (G5) is a separate download (scripts/nvidia-pack.sh,
# system/nvidia.go); mokutil asks the firmware to trust the orOS key that
# signs its modules when Secure Boot is on.
mokutil
